# conventions.list — which interactive surfaces answer to which convention class.
#
# Read by tools/gates/check-conventions.sh. The classes and their rows are the
# corpus at D:\dev\rag\ui-conventions\ — one file per gesture, each a numbered
# list of rules that every program in this class already follows.
#
# ===========================================================================
# WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR
# ===========================================================================
#
# The operator, 2026-08-20, after a fortnight of reporting conventions one at a
# time:
#
#   "I've never seen a program that doesn't live preview any change, and yet
#    here I am having to ask for all the minute details as if you'd never been
#    trained on it."
#
# The diagnosis is not missing knowledge. Asked directly, the answers come back
# right. The failure is that nothing PROMPTS the question while the code is
# being written — you are inside the local problem and the conventional
# expectation is never retrieved.
#
# So this is the prompt. A surface listed here must state, in its source, which
# rows of its class it satisfies and which it waives and why. The gate cannot
# check BEHAVIOUR — no grep can tell whether a preview tracks the pointer — but
# it can check that somebody consciously ANSWERED THE QUESTION, and it makes an
# unanswered one visible. That is exactly what was missing.
#
# Two precedents from the same day, both of which paid immediately:
#
#   * `the_keymap_offers_the_chords_a_document_application_must` asserts the
#     WHOLE LIST of universal chords rather than the one that was missing.
#     Ctrl+P had been absent for a fortnight and nothing had ever asked.
#   * `check-typing-guard.sh` found EIGHT further call sites the moment it first
#     ran — two of them live bugs, one of which would have deleted the
#     operator's selected object while he was mid-word.
#
# Neither was cleverness. Both were "write it down as a list and let a machine
# check it".
#
# ===========================================================================
# HOW A SURFACE DECLARES
# ===========================================================================
#
# A comment block anywhere in the file, one line per row of its class:
#
#     // conventions: drag-moves
#     // - D1 live-preview: the polyline follows the pointer, previewed from
#     //   `dimension_preview_segments` — the same function a committed
#     //   dimension is drawn from.
#     // - D3 escape-cancels: WAIVED — the gesture machine owns Escape and
#     //   abandons the pick; there is nothing for this module to do.
#
# Every row of the class must appear. `WAIVED` needs a reason on the same line
# or the next — a bare waiver is the exemption without the argument, which is
# how a checklist becomes theatre.
#
# ===========================================================================
# ADDING A SURFACE
# ===========================================================================
#
# When you build a new interactive surface, add it here. The gate cannot force
# that — nothing can grep "is this interactive" reliably — so it is a review
# obligation. What the gate CAN do, and does, is fail the moment a listed
# surface stops answering, which is when a class gains a row.
#
# ★ EVERY OPERATOR REPORT BECOMES A ROW. That is the compounding mechanism: a
# report currently costs an hour of their time and then evaporates. As a row it
# costs the same hour once and is checked forever — and the question stops being
# only "what do I fix" and becomes "which rule was I missing, and what else
# violates it?"
#
# Format: <path> <class>

crates/pdfcer-gui/src/canvas/selection/annot.rs      click-selects
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/canvas/clicking.rs             click-selects
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/canvas/dimdrag.rs              drag-moves
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/canvas/moving/mod.rs               drag-moves
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/canvas/resizing.rs             drag-moves
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/canvas/handledrag.rs           drag-moves
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/canvas/constrain.rs            drag-moves
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/canvas/handles.rs              handles
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/canvas/textedit/mod.rs         text-caret
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/canvas/textedit/caret.rs       text-caret
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/dialogs/print/mod.rs           dialogs
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/dialogs/insert_image.rs        dialogs
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/dialogs/scale.rs               dialogs
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/dialogs/export_image.rs        dialogs
crates/pdfcer-gui/src/dialogs/open_in_acrobat.rs   dialogs
